      "title": "TouchBridge: Tactile-Conditioned Human-to-Robot Transfer for Dexterous Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "TouchBridge addresses the problem that human demonstrations are a scalable data source for dexterous manipulation but sensing and hand-morphology differences hinder contact-rich transfer, and it tackles this with a hardware-software co-designed human-to-robot data pipeline whose Tac-Retarget component uses measured fingertip contact to align contact patches without object meshes, object-pose estimates, or physics simulation. Combined with visual synthesis and camera-anchored action conversion, it produces robot-domain demonstrations for fine-tuning a pretrained VLA model. Across four real-world contact-rich tasks, policies fine-tuned solely on converted human demonstrations reach 72.5% average success versus 77.5% with an equal number of teleoperated robot demonstrations, while collection is 7.0x faster, and Tac-Retarget outperforms DexPilot and UniDex by 25.0 and 42.5 percentage points under the same setup. Inspect how contact-patch correspondence is defined and how the no-simulation retargeting handles contact ambiguity.",
