      "canonical_paper_id": "openalex:W3185776277",
      "title": "Legged Robot State Estimation With Dynamic Contact Event Information",
      "takeaway": "This letter formulates legged-robot state estimation as a Maximum A Posteriori problem solved with Gauss-Newton, using Schur-complement marginalization to keep the problem fixed-size and deriving cost terms and Jacobians on the SO(3) manifold with a nominal-state plus variation reparameterization. It further proposes a slip rejection method to reduce errors from fault modeling of kinematics models. The algorithm is verified by comparison with the Invariant Extended Kalman Filter (IEKF) in real robot experiments across various environments, with the abstract reporting no numerical outcomes. The point to inspect is how slip rejection is triggered and how the MAP formulation and marginalization affect estimator behavior relative to the IEKF baseline.",
